First offset with |AUC-0.5| >= 0.08 : 3.00 s.
A 1.0 s window starting there covers [3.00, 4.00] s, so the cue onset
must lie inside that interval. CFG.cueOffsetSec = 3.00 s.
--> CONSISTENT.
The effect then persists to 7.50 s, i.e. roughly 4.5 s of imagery after
the cue, which matches the 4 s imagery period in the paradigm.
Do NOT read the argmax: imagery lasts seconds, so the peak is a tie inside
the plateau and moves around with noise. The ONSET is what locates the cue.
AUC below 0.5 only means C3 power goes DOWN for right-hand MI, which is
the textbook contralateral direction.

