contra-ipsi is taken from the SAME curves that are plotted.
"per-trial" normalises every trial to its own baseline first; it is a
different quantity and it is what the paired t-test (column p) operates on.
They can differ in size and occasionally in sign. Quoting one while plotting
the other is a mistake that is easy to make and hard to notice.
Correct lateralisation (contralateral more negative): 16 of 18 cells.
