============================================================================
SECTION 6 - PSD: band power = integrated PSD = covariance diagonal
============================================================================

Subject B04, 740 trials, window 0.5-3.5 s after the cue.

ch        mean(x_band^2)    integral of PSD     ratio   Pearson r   r vs cov diag
C3              5.49 uV2           6.10 uV2     1.112      0.9841          1.0000
Cz              3.80 uV2           4.22 uV2     1.112      0.9777          1.0000
C4              4.37 uV2           4.87 uV2     1.114      0.9871          1.0000

max |band power - covariance diagonal| / band power = 1.34e-03

The constant ratio is the FILTER, not a disagreement: an order-2
Butterworth is not a brick wall, so it already attenuates inside 8-30 Hz
while the Welch integral cuts sharply at the band edges. Because the
offset is CONSTANT it cancels exactly in (A-R)/R, which is why the ERD
percentage does not care which of the two is used.
The covariance diagonal is the same number to ~1e-3, and that diagonal
is what logvar_svm in s02_run_models.py classifies. These ERD curves and
that model read ONE physical quantity, computed two ways.

